### Alternative Concept and Complexity Analysis

Returning an index instead of a pointer:

```c
int findLowestIndex(int stock[], int n)
{
    int index = 0;

    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++)
    {
        if (stock[i] < stock[index])
            index = i;
    }

    return index;
}
```

* Time complexity: for both pointer and index methods.

* Space complexity: for both.

* Safety: An index is safer if an array is reallocated because the pointer may become invalid.
